    "summary": "Magical drum made of carved wood, membrane, bone and leather. A pear-shaped body, pierced with a double hole with a bone strip across the central divide and with leather thongs tied across it. The membrane sewn to the body and painted with various magical motifs. \r\n       Two early labels: \r\na) at the top a handwritten circular BM label recoring the number and donor: &#039;+4344  Lapland  Magical Drum.  H. Willett  3.6.89&#039;\r\nb) below a calligaphic label of laid paper, late 18th or early 19th century:  &#039;Lapland Magical Drum&#039;.",
